From fbe020447ced12096875735236e16c619695aad7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 22:56:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add c.d.f and w.r.t to base abbreviations

Add `c.d.f` to the base REFERENCE_ABBRVS and `w.r.t` to the base
INLINE_ONLY_ABBRVS so text such as "the c.d.f. F." or
"discussed w.r.t. V-TSMixer." is no longer split at the abbreviation.

Fixes #357
---
 CHANGELOG.md                    | 1 +
 CONTRIBUTORS.md                 | 1 +
 src/yasbd/rules/base.py         | 4 ++--
 tests/test_boundary_detector.py | 5 +++++
 4 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 2766be1..69b799c 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 ### Fixed
 
 - **Backtick-delimited quote sentence boundaries** ([#348](https://github.com/speedyk-005/yasbd-lib/pull/348)): Detect sentence boundaries after single/double backtick-delimited and doubled-apostrophe quoted text while preserving ordinary contractions.
+- **Missing `c.d.f.` and `w.r.t.` base abbreviations** ([#NNN](https://github.com/speedyk-005/yasbd-lib/pull/NNN)): Add `c.d.f` to the base reference abbreviations and `w.r.t` to the base inline-only abbreviations so they no longer cause false sentence splits.
 
 ...
 
